[
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span> has recently been pushing for bug reports and more generally any code block to come with informations/warnings/errors written as docstrings in <code>#guards_msgs</code>. It is however currently extremely painful to create such a code block because of how picky <code>#guard_msgs</code> is about whitespace, etc, and anyway why should I be copy-pasting code into code instead of a code action doing this for me?</p>",
        "id": 591380186,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777382409
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would it therefore be possible for a failing <code>#guard_msgs</code> to come with a self-updating code action instead of the diff view?</p>",
        "id": 591380518,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777382463
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Or both, as maybe some find the diff helpful still?</p>",
        "id": 591380833,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1777382535
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I there not already a code action for <code>#guard_msgs</code>?</p>",
        "id": 591381425,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1777382659
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>at least shows a code action for me</p>",
        "id": 591381567,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1777382688
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Where is it in the following?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ring</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591382189,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777382831
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For me, it shows after the code block.</p>",
        "id": 591382382,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1777382881
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"409x203\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/GTuu2EDI8Z_qHhDkaff4T40U/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/GTuu2EDI8Z_qHhDkaff4T40U/image.png/840x560.webp\"><br>\nIn fact, it depends on where I put my cursor. Sometimes it is above, sometimes below.</p>",
        "id": 591382438,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1777382895
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah! so it is not a code action in the infoview, which is where I would have expected it</p>",
        "id": 591382764,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777382970
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Given that I have spent months writing <code>#guard_msgs</code> docstrings by hand without ever seeing this code action, is there any chance we could make it more discoverable? <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 591383009,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1777383018
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, I did not know there is a distinction. I just do <code>&lt;leader&gt;a</code> in neovim for all code actions.</p>",
        "id": 591383310,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1777383075
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>for me (in vscode), i just move my cursor to the thing, press <code>ctrl+.</code> to show the actions, and select the right one from there</p>",
        "id": 591383880,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777383196
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Wow you're all so fancy! I just click the blue thingy.</p>",
        "id": 591461355,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1777402614
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I (in vscode) just press <code>ctrl+.</code> twice in a row to execute the code action.</p>",
        "id": 591471988,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777406038
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Perhaps the code action should use the <code>#guard_msgs</code> as the range of its suggestion, rather than the entire command?</p>",
        "id": 591598679,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777412495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That is, I think <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/3dc1a088b6d2d8eafe25a7cd7ec7b58d731bd7cc/src/Lean/Elab/GuardMsgs.lean#L244\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/3dc1a088b6d2d8eafe25a7cd7ec7b58d731bd7cc/src/Lean/Elab/GuardMsgs.lean#L244</a> should be <code>tk</code> instead of <code>← getRef</code></p>",
        "id": 591613159,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777412967
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would that mean that you can only execute the code action with your cursor on <code>#guard_msgs</code>? I quite enjoy being able to use the code action from anywhere - either the doc-string, or anywhere else in the command</p>",
        "id": 591616691,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1777413066
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, good point</p>",
        "id": 591623162,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777413251
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Semi-related: is there a way to guard a message that contains <code>/-</code> as a substring?</p>",
        "id": 591720749,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777451600
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>just the same, no? the following works:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Type mismatch</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  \"/- -/</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">has type</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">  String</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">but is expected to have type</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">  Nat</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">#guard_msgs in</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">def foo (x : U) : Nat := \"</span><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> -/</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591755231,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777459749
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>syntax highlighting doesn't, but this works on live lean...</p>",
        "id": 591755338,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777459776
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the correct version of this question is: what if we replaced that string by \"-/\"?</p>",
        "id": 591758523,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1777460578
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"684366\">@Edward van de Meent</span> Try not to include the matching <code>-/</code>.</p>",
        "id": 591761533,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1777461513
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"thinking\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f914\" role=\"img\" title=\"thinking\">:thinking:</span></p>",
        "id": 591761748,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777461571
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess this is what Damiano means?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Type mismatch</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  \"bla/-bla\"</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">has type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  String</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">but is expected to have type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Nat</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bla/-bla\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Which gives the error <code>unterminated comment</code>.<br>\n(And funnily, the Zulip syntax highligthing is <del>better than</del> [see below!] the one on <a href=\"http://live.lean-lang.org\">live.lean-lang.org</a> for this.</p>",
        "id": 591767161,
        "sender_full_name": "Malvin Gattinger",
        "timestamp": 1777463008
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>how so? it's clearly not displaying it the way it gets parsed by lean, so arguably it's less informative?</p>",
        "id": 591767846,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777463185
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>True. \"better\" in this case is just \"looking how we would want it to be parsed\" but is more like \"more misleading\" <span aria-label=\"thinking\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f914\" role=\"img\" title=\"thinking\">:thinking:</span></p>",
        "id": 591808196,
        "sender_full_name": "Malvin Gattinger",
        "timestamp": 1777471773
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why would you want your syntax highlighting to disagree with the way that something is being parsed? if anything that is only going to add more confusion as opposed to helping resolve the confusion.</p>",
        "id": 591818027,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1777473884
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, sorry. What I meant is \"the syntax highlighting is showing how we would want Lean to parse this\", but maybe it is impossible to get Lean to parse it like that? And the separate question: is it possible to write a correct guard message docstring for this example?</p>",
        "id": 591832322,
        "sender_full_name": "Malvin Gattinger",
        "timestamp": 1777477248
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"422703\">Malvin Gattinger</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Autogenerate.20docstring.20for.20.23guards_msgs/near/591832322\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And the separate question: is it possible to write a correct guard message docstring for this example?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You can do this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">docstr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"error: Type mismatch</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">  </span><span class=\"se\">\\\"</span><span class=\"s2\">bla/-bla</span><span class=\"se\">\\\"\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">has type</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">  String</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">but is expected to have type</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">  Nat</span><span class=\"se\">\\n</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- see `MathlibTest/willRoundTrip`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkDocComment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">String</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TSyntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Command.docComment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkNode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Parser.Command.docComment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mkAtom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"/--\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkAtom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"-/\"</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"guardstr\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mkDocComment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">docstr</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"n\">docComment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">cmd</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">guardstr</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">U</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bla/-bla\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591837912,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777478617
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Since we're sharing keyboard shortcuts, I do the \"I'm feeling lucky\" command, <code>⌥⌘.</code> (Preferred Quick Fix). I'm not sure what it is on other platforms, but it's what VS Code suggests to me when I hover over the lightbulb. (I also have no idea whether or not it's \"preferred\" since it's marked as preferred somewhere, or if it's figured out I prefer it!)</p>",
        "id": 591847515,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1777481049
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"321459\">Damiano Testa</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Autogenerate.20docstring.20for.20.23guards_msgs/near/591720749\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Semi-related: is there a way to guard a message that contains <code>/-</code> as a substring?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It seems like a reasonable request that <code>#guard_msgs</code> should have a way to escape these (and should automatically escape them for you!). It already uses <code>⏎</code> to escape trailing whitespace for example.</p>\n<p>It's too bad that <code>--</code> doesn't cancel out <code>-/</code> in the same line, otherwise I might suggest that <code>#guard_msgs</code> create and understand output like the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-- error: Type mismatch</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">--   \"/- -/</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">-- has type</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">--   String</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">-- but is expected to have type</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">--   Nat</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">#guard_msgs in</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">def foo (x : U) : Nat := \"</span><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> -/</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This seems, possibly, like a reasonable change to comment lexical syntax.</p>",
        "id": 591847832,
        "sender_full_name": "Kyle Miller",
        "timestamp": 1777481142
    }
]